# ==============================================================================
# Build context exclusions
# ==============================================================================
#
# This file MUST live at the root of the build context, which the
# compose files set to the repository root. A .dockerignore sitting next
# to the Dockerfile is not read for a root context, so the one in
# infra/docker/backend/ had no effect at all - and `COPY backend/ .`
# was baking .env, .venv and .git straight into the image.
#
# Anything excluded here is invisible to COPY, so secrets cannot reach a
# layer even by accident.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.env
infra/nginx/certs/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# .git is often the largest thing in the context and can contain deleted
# secrets that are still in history.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.venv/
**/.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Django runtime output
#
# Rebuilt inside the image; copying them in wastes layers and can shadow
# a fresh collectstatic.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**/staticfiles/
**/media/
**/logs/
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.log

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend
#
# node_modules alone can be hundreds of megabytes of build context that
# the backend image never uses.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docs and compose
#
# Not needed at runtime.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

docker-compose*.yml
**/docs/
README.md

.tools
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/logs
backups
infra/nginx/certs

**/.pnpm-store/

.deployment/
infra/e2e/generated/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/

**/.aws/
**/.ssh/
**/.terraform/
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.netrc
**/credentials.json
**/*.credentials.json
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup
